IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tasjcxv-dates`
IMPORT `tasjcxv-claims`

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (Tas) -- cases for every exported question.
-- Expected values worked by hand from the deposited text (../../registers/source-bundle/act-1987-078.txt), section by
-- section, never copied from the encoding's output. Edges: the s 3/3A exclusions on every question that carries them,
-- each limb of each "where", the last day of the time a court directs (s 6(5)(b)) and the day after, a notice before the
-- direction, each court pair in s 5, each appeal route in s 7.
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026, (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Cases`

§§ `s 3, s 3A`

#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a civil proceeding, which this Act's rules on transfer, removal and appeal can reach (s 3)`
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a criminal proceeding is not a "proceeding" under this Act (s 3(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: this Act does not apply to the jurisdiction that Division 1 of Part 9.6A of the Corporations Act 2001 deals with (s 3A, the text's no)`
-- Both: the criminal exclusion is reported first.
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a criminal proceeding is not a "proceeding" under this Act (s 3(1), the text's no)`

-- s 3(1) "State matter": either limb.
#ASSERT `a State matter` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `a State matter` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`a State matter` FALSE FALSE))

-- s 3(2): the Family Court of Western Australia is read into "the Supreme Court of another State".
#ASSERT `a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `the Family Court of Western Australia`
#ASSERT `a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory`
#ASSERT (NOT (`a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `the Federal Court of Australia`))

§§ `s 4`

-- A Tasmanian common law claim (own jurisdiction), heard by the Supreme Court of Victoria: s 4(3).
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Tasmania hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `yes: that Supreme Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your State matter (s 4(3))`
-- Removed under s 8 only: still a State matter (s 3(1)(b)); the Family Court of WA: s 4(4).
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Tasmania hear my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `a State Family Court of another State` EQUALS `yes: that State Family Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your State matter (s 4(4))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Tasmania hear my matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `no: s 4 gives no jurisdiction in criminal matters (s 4(5), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Tasmania hear my matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `no: this Act does not apply to the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A, the text's no) -- s 4`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Tasmania hear my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `s 4 gives it nothing: your matter is not a State matter (s 3(1)), and this Act does not say more (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Tasmania hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Federal Court or the Family Court of Australia (a federal court)` EQUALS `s 4 gives it nothing: s 4(3) and (4) vest jurisdiction in the Supreme Courts and State Family Courts of other States and Territories, not in a federal court; the former s 4(1) and (2) are omitted (NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 5 and s 6A`

-- s 5(1): Tasmania to the Federal Court, "more appropriate".
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court of Tasmania must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court (s 5(1))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Family Court of Australia` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court of Tasmania must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court (s 5(1))`
-- s 5(1) has no "otherwise in the interests of justice" limb (finding 2): the "where" fails.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds neither` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 5(2): Tasmania to another Supreme Court, either limb; and to the Family Court of WA (s 3(2)).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court of Tasmania must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court of Tasmania must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Family Court of Western Australia` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court of Tasmania must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` `the court finds neither` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 5(3): another Supreme Court to Tasmania.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: that Supreme Court must transfer it to the Supreme Court of Tasmania (s 5(3))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the court finds neither` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 5(4): a federal court to Tasmania.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Federal Court of Australia` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Federal Court or the Family Court must transfer it to the Supreme Court of Tasmania (s 5(4))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Family Court of Australia` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the court finds neither` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 6A(3), (4): a federal matter proceeding in Tasmania.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not required by s 5(1) or s 6 (s 6A(3), the text's no), but the Supreme Court may transfer it, and it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice (s 6A(4))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds neither` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(1) and s 6 do not require it (s 6A(3), the text's no), and the court does not consider transfer appropriate (s 6A(4))`
-- One limb of s 6A(1) missing: not a federal matter proceeding, back to s 5(1).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court of Tasmania must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court (s 5(1))`
-- s 6A(2): a federal matter proceeding in a federal court.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Federal Court of Australia` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice that the other court decide it` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `may: s 5(4) does not apply (s 6A(2)), but the Federal Court or the Family Court may transfer it to the Supreme Court, and it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Family Court of Australia` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the court finds neither` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(4) does not apply (s 6A(2), the text's no), and the court does not consider transfer appropriate`
-- Pairs this Act does not cover.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `the Federal Court of Australia` `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of another State may (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `another court or tribunal` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of another State may (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` TRUE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE TRUE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5`

-- s 6A(1): all four limbs.
#ASSERT `s 6A(1) -- a federal matter proceeding` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 6A(1) -- a federal matter proceeding` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 6A(1) -- a federal matter proceeding` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 6A(1) -- a federal matter proceeding` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))

-- s 5(6)
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer your related proceeding to the same court (s 5(6))`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(6) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(6) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 5(6) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5(6)`

-- s 5(7)
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am the plaintiff, applicant or claimant` EQUALS `yes: as a party you may apply for the transfer (s 5(7)); the court may also act of its own motion or on an Attorney-General's application`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am the defendant or respondent` EQUALS `yes: as a party you may apply for the transfer (s 5(7)); the court may also act of its own motion or on an Attorney-General's application`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I have intervened in the proceeding` EQUALS `yes: a person who intervenes is a party (s 3(1)), so you may apply for the transfer (s 5(7))`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am not a party and have not intervened` EQUALS `s 5(7) names no application by you: it names a party, the court of its own motion and the Attorneys-General (NOTHING-kind)`

-- s 5(8)
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: your lawyer may practise in the other court in this proceeding as in a federal court exercising federal jurisdiction (s 5(8))`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 5(8) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 5(8) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 5(8) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`

§§ `s 6`

#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court -- so much of it as is, in the court's opinion, within the Federal Court's jurisdiction, including its accrued jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1A), (2)(a))`
-- Paragraph (c) or (e), not a federal matter proceeding: the Federal Court.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (c) or (e) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court -- so much of it as is, in the court's opinion, within the Federal Court's jurisdiction, including its accrued jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1A), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (ab) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to whichever of the Family Court of Australia, the Family Court of Western Australia and the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory it thinks appropriate -- so much of it as is within that court's jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1A), (2)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `another paragraph of the Commonwealth Act's definition, which s 6(2) does not name` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, the Supreme Court must transfer it (s 6(1)); but s 6(2) names no court for a matter under that paragraph of the Commonwealth definition (NOTHING-kind as to where)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Supreme Court has ordered that it decide the proceeding itself (s 6(1)(b), (3); the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 6 does not apply to this appeal in the Full Court, because the court below made an order under s 6(3) (or the former s 6(1)) (s 6(9), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (c) or (e) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not required: s 6 does not require the transfer of a federal matter proceeding while the related State matter proceeding is pending in a Tasmanian court (s 6A(3), the text's no); the Supreme Court may still transfer it if it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice (s 6A(4))`
-- The same s 6A facts with a paragraph (a) matter: s 6A does not reach it.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court -- so much of it as is, in the court's opinion, within the Federal Court's jurisdiction, including its accrued jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1A), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `no special federal matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 6 does not arise: no special federal matter, or the proceeding is not pending in the Supreme Court of Tasmania (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 6 does not arise: no special federal matter, or the proceeding is not pending in the Supreme Court of Tasmania (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` TRUE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth Act's definition` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 6`

-- s 6(3), (4)
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order that it decide the proceeding itself (s 6(3)); it must weigh the general rule that special federal matters should be heard by the Federal Court or a court in s 6(2)(b), and any Attorney-General's submission (s 6(6))`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before written notice of the special federal matter has been given to both the Commonwealth and the Tasmanian Attorney-General (s 6(4)(a), the text's no); the court may adjourn and direct a party to give it (s 6(5))`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before written notice of the special federal matter has been given to both the Commonwealth and the Tasmanian Attorney-General (s 6(4)(a), the text's no); the court may adjourn and direct a party to give it (s 6(5))`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before a reasonable time has passed since the notice for the Attorneys-General to consider making submissions (s 6(4)(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the court is not satisfied that there are special reasons, other than the parties' convenience, for it to decide the proceeding (s 6(3), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 6(3) does not arise: no special federal matter pending in the Supreme Court of Tasmania (the text's no)`

-- s 6(5)(b): directed on 1 October 2026, 14 days allowed: the last day is 15 October 2026 (day 14, fork F7).
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 15 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 20 10 2026) EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 16 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 20 10 2026) EQUALS `no: the notice was not given within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); until both Attorneys-General have it, the Supreme Court cannot order that it keep the proceeding (s 6(4))`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
-- Given before the direction (fork F11).
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) 14 TRUE (`the calendar date` 28 9 2026) (`the calendar date` 20 10 2026) EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
-- Not given: on the last day still in time, the day after not.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) 14 FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 15 10 2026) EQUALS `not yet, but still in time: the time the court directed has not run out (s 6(5)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) 14 FALSE (`the calendar date` 1 1 2000) (`the calendar date` 16 10 2026) EQUALS `no: the notice was not given within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); until both Attorneys-General have it, the Supreme Court cannot order that it keep the proceeding (s 6(4))`
-- Across a month end: directed 25 February 2027, 7 days: last day 4 March 2027.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 25 2 2027) 7 TRUE (`the calendar date` 4 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2027) EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` (`the calendar date` 25 2 2027) 7 TRUE (`the calendar date` 5 3 2027) (`the calendar date` 10 3 2027) EQUALS `no: the notice was not given within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); until both Attorneys-General have it, the Supreme Court cannot order that it keep the proceeding (s 6(4))`

#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 14 14
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 14 15))
#ASSERT `the days from` (`the calendar date` 25 2 2027) `to` (`the calendar date` 4 3 2027) EQUALS 7

-- expect: FULFILLED (notice on the last day)
#TRACE `s 6(5)(b) -- give the notice within the time the court directed` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the directed party` DOES `give written notice of the special federal matter to both Attorneys-General` AT 14

-- expect: BREACH by the directed party (notice on day 15)
#TRACE `s 6(5)(b) -- give the notice within the time the court directed` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the directed party` DOES `give written notice of the special federal matter to both Attorneys-General` AT 15

-- s 6(7)
#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: nothing in s 6 stops the Supreme Court granting urgent interlocutory relief, as it is in the interests of justice (s 6(7))`
#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 6(7) does not save it: the court does not find the relief in the interests of justice (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 6(7) does not reach it: it speaks only of urgent relief of an interlocutory nature (NOTHING-kind)`

-- s 6(8), s 7(7)
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 6 invalidates the decision (s 6(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without the s 6(4) notice being given` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 6 invalidates the decision (s 6(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(7) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Full Court went on under s 7(6) (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Full Court decided an appeal that s 7(4) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 7 invalidates the decision (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Full Court decided an appeal that s 7(4) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 7 invalidates the decision (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Full Court decided an appeal that s 7(4) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(7) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Full Court went on under s 7(6) (NOTHING-kind)`

§§ `s 7`

#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Federal Court` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal from a single judge of the Federal Court or the Family Court shall not be instituted in the Full Court of the Supreme Court (s 7(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Family Court of Australia` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal from a single judge of the Federal Court or the Family Court shall not be instituted in the Full Court of the Supreme Court (s 7(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Federal Court` `the Full Court of the Family Court of Australia` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal shall not be instituted from the Federal Court or the Family Court to the other of them (s 7(2), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Family Court of Australia` `the Full Court of the Federal Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal shall not be instituted from the Federal Court or the Family Court to the other of them (s 7(2), the text's no)`
-- Within one federal court: this Act is silent.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Federal Court` `the Full Court of the Federal Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say where this appeal goes (NOTHING-kind)`
-- s 7(3)
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: with no matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal is instituted in the Full Court of the Supreme Court and only there (s 7(3))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Full Court of the Federal Court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: with no matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal must be instituted only in the Full Court of the Supreme Court (s 7(3), the text's no)`
-- s 7(4)
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Full Court of the Federal Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal goes only to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(4))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the High Court, with special leave` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal goes only to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(4))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal must go to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(4), the text's no)`
-- s 7(5)
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a judge of a State Family Court` `the Full Court of the Family Court of Australia` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the appeal may be dealt with as if no matter in it arose under a Schedule Act (s 7(5))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `a decision of a judge of a State Family Court` `the Full Court of the Family Court of Australia` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say where this appeal goes (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `some other decision` `some other court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say where this appeal goes (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` TRUE FALSE `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of Tasmania` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 7`

-- s 7(6)
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Full Court of the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires (s 7(6))`
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the interests of justice require the Full Court to go on and decide it (s 7(6)); its decision is not invalid under s 7 (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 7(6) does not arise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 7(6) does not arise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

§§ `s 8`

#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `a Tasmanian court other than the Supreme Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order it removed to itself, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 8(1)); this Act then applies to it as if it were a proceeding in the Supreme Court (s 8(2)), which may later send it back (s 8(3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `a tribunal established by or under an Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order it removed to itself, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 8(1)); this Act then applies to it as if it were a proceeding in the Supreme Court (s 8(2)), which may later send it back (s 8(3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `a tribunal established by or under an Act` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 8 does not allow removal on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court of Tasmania, or a court outside Tasmania` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 8 does not allow removal on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE TRUE `a Tasmanian court other than the Supreme Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 8`

§§ `s 10`

#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court it is in may transfer it to that lower Tasmanian court, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 10)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 10`

§§ `s 11 and s 12`

#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the written and unwritten law of the other State or Territory under whose written law your right of action arises (s 11(1)(b)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the law in force in the State or Territory where the court is sitting, including its choice of law rules (s 11(1)(a)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 11(1) does not apply: the court will not be exercising cross-vested jurisdiction (the text's no: its "where" fails); this Act does not say which law applies`

#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- do the steps already taken count in the new court` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the new court deals with the proceeding as if the steps taken in the old court, including its orders, had been taken in the new court, subject to any order of the new court (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- do the steps already taken count in the new court` FALSE EQUALS `s 11(3) does not apply: the proceeding was not transferred or removed (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the new court may make an order about the costs of the proceeding before the transfer or removal (s 12)`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: those costs have already been dealt with by another court (s 12, the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 12 does not apply: the proceeding was not transferred or removed (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

§§ `s 13 and s 14`

#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `a decision about transferring or removing my proceeding under this Act` EQUALS `no: no appeal lies from a decision about the transfer or removal of a proceeding under this Act (s 13(a), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `a decision under s 11(1) about which rules of evidence and procedure apply` EQUALS `no: no appeal lies from a decision about which rules of evidence and procedure apply under s 11(1) (s 13(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `some other decision in my proceeding` EQUALS `s 13 does not bar an appeal from it; whether one lies is for other law (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 14(2) -- can I enforce the judgment in Tasmania` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the judgment is enforceable in Tasmania as if given entirely in the Supreme Court's own jurisdiction (s 14(2))`
#ASSERT `s 14(2) -- can I enforce the judgment in Tasmania` `the Supreme Court of Tasmania` FALSE EQUALS `s 14(2) does not reach it: it covers only a judgment of the Supreme Court of Tasmania given in whole or in part in cross-vested jurisdiction (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 14(2) -- can I enforce the judgment in Tasmania` `the Federal Court of Australia` TRUE EQUALS `s 14(2) does not reach it: it covers only a judgment of the Supreme Court of Tasmania given in whole or in part in cross-vested jurisdiction (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Tasmanian law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: that provision is read as referring to the court that did the thing (s 14(3))`
#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Tasmanian law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 14(3) does not reach a law relating to the enforcement of judgments (s 14(3)(a), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Tasmanian law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 14(3) does not apply on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Tasmanian law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 14(3) does not apply on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
